**Theorem 1.5 (combined target).** Under Assumption 1.2, the original
initialization of §2 has the following property. At each authentic
completed predecessor, every accepted legacy or general GCA target is
carried through actual received bodies

$$
S(h_k)\longrightarrow B(h_k)\longrightarrow M_J(h_k)
\longrightarrow T(h_k)\longrightarrow S(h_k).
$$

Each body represents its independently defined natural object on the
same incidence carrier. Each receiver independently decodes and checks
its received body; the final independently decoded value passes the
original history Image checker, and exactly one outer history item and
one final Ready complete the flight. Each finite target in $[a,b]$ has an
actually supplyable finite AcquisitionOffset name. Every completed
returning seven-tag source call has the SourceOffset names of all its
cuts, without a strict-Reserve assumption. All initialization, access,
conversion, check and return work is retained and priced. The proof is
given in §§2–8. The original-task consequence is exactly §9, with the
remaining obligations in §10.

